course: dictionary
lesson: 4707
title: Honk: one word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: The word honk can be a verb (to honk) or a noun (a honk). It has more than one meaning, so the words around it tell you which one you need. Context is the clue.
explain: «The hammer-headed bat is the largest bat in Africa, and males have huge heads to make loud honking calls that females listen to.» Here honking means a loud call that an animal makes, not a car horn. The clues are calls and females listen.
explain: «Parasaurolophus had a long hollow crest that probably worked like a trumpet, making deep honking sounds.» The words like a trumpet tell you honking is a loud, deep sound. Check by swapping in your meaning: making deep loud sounds. It still makes sense.
explain: On the road, drivers honk to warn people or other cars. If you hear a honk near you, it can mean danger, so stop and look.
fact: Honk means to make the loud sound of a car horn, or the loud cry a goose makes.
fact: As a noun, a honk is one such sound: «a honk of geese» is a phrase about a group of geese.
fact: As a verb, honk shows an action: «honk the horn» and «honk at someone».
fact: Geese honk when they fly in a V shape.
fact: A honk near you can mean danger, so stop and look.
exercise: «Parasaurolophus had a long hollow crest that probably worked like a trumpet, making deep honking sounds.» What does honking mean here? | A soft whisper | *A loud, deep sound | A bright colour | A kind of food
exercise: In the phrase «a honk of geese», is honk a verb or a noun? | *Noun | Adverb | Adjective | Verb
exercise: Which sound does a goose make? | Neigh | Bark | *Honk | Purr
test: Which animal in the sentences uses a hollow crest to make honking sounds? | Hammer-headed bat | Ancient castle | *Parasaurolophus | Car horn
test: Why do drivers honk on the road? | To ask for a song | *To warn people or other cars | To count the trees | To cook dinner
exam: In which sentence is honk a noun? | Honk the horn if you see the bus | The geese honk as they fly over the lake | Drivers honk to warn other cars | *A honk from the car made me jump
